 "finding": "The published method's picture does not follow the room's depth. Over simulated desert shaking at Giza's measured microseism level, on the real dwell, with a depth axis from 0 to 41 m, the change each room's imprint makes to the picture (each boosted to 2 rad of phase over the room) spreads over the whole axis: the 15 m room puts 16% of it between 12 and 18 m and the 30 m room 16% between 27 and 33 m, where 15% and 15% of the axis lie; their largest changes sit at 13.9 m and 13.7 m, and their depth profiles correlate at 0.76. A granite block where the hollow room was changes the picture over the room with a map that correlates with the hollow room's at -0.45 (the null, random phases at the same pixels: 0.15), as their marks on the ground correlate at -0.88 before any method reads them: the picture carries the surface's motion, sign and all, spread over every depth (depth profiles correlating at 0.41). Stated before the run, a depth imager would gather each room's change at its depth; neither room's does. The imprints came from the lab's solver settling under a uniform strain; for the hollow 15 m room its peak is 1.000 of P2-04's (a larger domain)."
